46899261530387,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":76.2,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.019275574424071587,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5057950150833852,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":15.7,"_gate_incr_roic":0.056742150664739054,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":35.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.008744649828014303,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":30.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.17914805491296693,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.23866457910981675,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.00834558442499192,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":58.3,"_gate_fund_growth":0.06252278498174074,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":62.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.005136797252969828,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":16.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.013072856278342426,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":33.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013158007023292926,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.013250001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Construction Partners, Inc., a civil infrastructure company, constructs and maintains roadways in Alabama, Florida, Georgia, North Carolina, Oklahoma, South Carolina, Tennessee, and Texas. The company provides various products and services to public and private infrastructure projects, such as highways, roads, bridges, airports, and commercial and residential developments. It also engages in manufacturing and distributing hot mix asphalt (HMA) for internal use and sales to third parties in connection with construction projects; and paving activities, including the construction of roadway base layers and application of asphalt pavement. In addition, the company is involved in site development, including the installation of utility and drainage systems; mining aggregates, such as sand, gravel, and construction stones that are used as raw materials in the production of HMA; and distributing liquid asphalt cement for internal use and sales to third parties in connection with HMA production. The company was formerly known as SunTx CPI Growth Company, Inc. and changed its name to Construction Partners, Inc. in September 2017. Construction Partners, Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in Dothan, Alabama.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Fred J. Smith III | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $94K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $23K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Construction Partners, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.6B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +29% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $153M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Construction Partners, Inc. $ROAD Stock: Van Berkom & Associates Inc. Raises Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/construction-partners-inc-road-stock-van-berkom-associates-inc-raises-holdings.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794308715.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Construction Partners (ROAD) Could Be 44% Undervalued On Record 2026 Results And 2027 Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-road/construction-partners/news/construction-partners-road-could-be-44-undervalued-on-record","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794069026.726,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Ned N. Fleming IV Reports Acquisition of 5,532 Shares and Tax Withholding Surrender at Construction Partners (NASDAQ:ROAD)","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/ned-n-fleming-iv-reports-acquisition-of-5532-shares-and-tax-withholding-surrender-at-construction-partners-nasdaqroad","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794002458.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Construction Partners (NASDAQ:ROAD) Shares Gap Down \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/construction-partners-nasdaqroad-shares-gap-down-time-to-sell.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793901682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How 2027 Earnings Guidance At Construction Partners Stock Has Changed Its Investment Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-road/construction-partners/news/how-2027-earnings-guidance-at-construction-partners-stock-ha","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572757.802,"o